# Linear tickets from chat (Phase ①)

Part of **`captain-dev-workflow.mdc`**. Ticket comes **before** Lavish plan and build.

When the captain asks to **create**, **file**, **log**, or **open** a Linear ticket
—or describes any work/bug/idea without saying **"no ticket"**— **create the issue**
first. Do not jump to planning or coding.

## Protocol

1. Read folder routing: `docs/linear-ticket-system.md` (decision tree + projects).
2. Parse: title, bug vs feature, portal, area, urgency.
3. **Create** via `npm run linear:ticket -- --chat "<captain's words>"` (GraphQL API only).
4. Reply with **PRP-###** and the **full Linear URL**.
5. **Next:** Phase ② — `npm run lavish:plan` (see `captain-dev-workflow.mdc`).

**Do not use Linear MCP** — `LINEAR_API_KEY` in `.env.local` is required.

## Chat triggers (examples)

- "Create a ticket: calendar UI needs work"
- "File this bug in Linear — residents tab crashes"
- "Log a feature request for SMS applications"
- "Ticket:" / "Linear:" prefix

## Routing (auto)

| Captain mentions… | Project | Milestone |
| --- | --- | --- |
| production, resend, cron, env | 01 — Infrastructure & Ops | Production env / email |
| manager portal, /portal/ | 02 — Manager Portal | matching section |
| resident, /resident/ | 03 — Resident Portal | matching section |
| SMS, inbox, email | 06 — Communication Hub | SMS or Email & Inbox |
| lease, application | 07 — Leases & Applications | … |
| payment, stripe, charge | 08 — Payments & Finance | Charges & ledger |
| assistant, AI | 09 — AI Assistant | Manager assistant |
| listing, wizard | 10 — Listings & Properties | Create wizard |
| calendar, tour | 11 — Calendar & Tours | Manager calendar UI |

Always add labels: `portal:*`, `area:*`, and `Bug` | `Feature` | `Improvement`.

Assignee + priority are auto-inferred (`scripts/linear/triage-rules.mjs`).

## Title format

`[Area] Short imperative — user-visible outcome`

## Do not

- Use Linear MCP or `cursor agent` for tickets.
- Create tickets without project + milestone.
- Put secrets in descriptions.

## Auth

`LINEAR_API_KEY` in `.env.local` — https://linear.app/settings/api
